@startuml 16-pattern-adapter
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title Design pattern 5 — Adapter (interchangeable GPS sources in the driver app)

class "Driver app\n(public/js/driver.js)" as DriverApp <<client>>
interface "GpsSource\n(conceptual contract —\nnot declared in code)" as GpsSource <<duck-typed>> {
  +kind: 'device' | 'simulator'
  +start(onFix: (fix) => void, onError: (err) => void): void
  +stop(): void
}
class DeviceGps <<adapter>> {
  -watchId: number | null
  -minIntervalMs: number
  +start(onFix, onError): void
  +stop(): void
}
class SimulatedGps <<simulated source>> {
  -along: number
  -speedKmh: number
  +outage: boolean
  +dwelling: boolean
  +start(onFix): void
  +stop(): void
  +setSpeed(kmh: number): void
  +setOutage(on: boolean): void
  +glitchFix(): fix
}
class "navigator.geolocation\n(browser Geolocation API)" as Geo <<adaptee>> {
  +watchPosition(success, error, options): number
  +clearWatch(id: number): void
}
class "Route geometry\n(path points, stops, dwell time)" as Geometry
class LocationUploader {
  +queue: fix[]
  +networkDown: boolean
  -backoffMs: number
  +push(fix): void
  +setNetworkDown(down: boolean): void
  +pause(): void
  +resume(): void
  +drain(timeoutMs: number): Promise<boolean>
  +flush(): Promise<void>
  +status(): {state, queued, dropped, ...}
  +stop(): void
}

DriverApp --> "0..1" GpsSource : gps (null when no trip, or after a reload\nuntil the driver chooses a source)
DriverApp --> "0..1" LocationUploader : push(fix) from the onFix callback
DriverApp ..> SimulatedGps : demo controls\n(setSpeed, setOutage, glitchFix)
GpsSource <|.. DeviceGps
GpsSource <|.. SimulatedGps
DeviceGps --> Geo : adapts
SimulatedGps --> Geometry : generates positions from

note bottom of GpsSource
  JavaScript has no interfaces: GpsSource is the contract described in
  the header comment of public/js/gps.js, satisfied by duck typing.
  Problem solved: the system must be demonstrable without shuttles,
  but the demo must exercise exactly the same upload path as a real
  phone. The code that runs a trip uses only start/stop; the demo
  control panel additionally calls SimulatedGps-only operations.
  DeviceGps is the true adapter (it converts the browser Geolocation
  API to the contract); SimulatedGps is an alternative implementation
  of the same contract. The server processes both sources the same way;
  each stored position keeps its "source" for the record and so that a
  reloaded driver page resumes the source the trip was really using.
end note
@enduml
